  <justification component="Unedited-original save branch (extends existing save path)">
    <existing>The save path already regenerates via `tipTapToDocxBytes`; the editor already reports dirty; original upload bytes are retained by the 012/010 mount.</existing>
    <extension>Add a dirty-state conditional that persists retained original bytes when clean; no new service.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, saving an untouched upload runs it through the lossy mammoth round-trip and mangles formatting the user never edited — a concrete fidelity regression FR-06a exists to prevent.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load spec.md FR-06a. Read the save path (`PromoteIfEphemeralAsync` + client save), `tipTapToDocxBytes`, and the dirty-tracking channel.</step>
    <step order="1">Ensure the retained original upload bytes are available at Save time (from the 010/012 mount).</step>
    <step order="2">Branch on editor dirty state: clean -&gt; persist retained original bytes byte-identical; dirty -&gt; persist regenerated `.docx` via the existing path.</step>
    <step order="3">Persist to the container resolved by create-on-save (013) through the SpeFileStore facade.</step>
    <step order="4">Add tests: unedited save byte-identical to upload; edited save reflects edits. Build BFF + package; measure publish-size; CVE scan.</step>
    <step order="5">Run code-review + adr-check (Step 9.5). Update TASK-INDEX + current-task.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/ComposeServiceUploadFidelityTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Upload -&gt; Save without editing persists SPE bytes byte-identical to the uploaded file.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Upload -&gt; edit -&gt; Save persists a regenerated `.docx` reflecting the edits (existing path).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The branch keys off the editor's dirty state; a clean editor never triggers regeneration.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Persistence targets the container resolved by create-on-save (013) via the SpeFileStore facade; no `Microsoft.Graph` leak (ADR-007).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(negative) A whitespace-only / no-op edit that does not set dirty still persists the original (no spurious regeneration).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish-size delta reported vs 49.63 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE; unit tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>

  <notes>
    Implemented as a CLIENT-side branch (directional deviation, grounded in code): the retained
    original bytes are ALREADY held for the whole mount lifetime in `ComposeWorkspace`'s
    `state.docxBytes` (set once by the `loadSucceeded`/`mountTransient` reducer actions and never
    mutated by any other action — verified by reading `ComposeWorkspace.types.ts`), so no new
    plumbing was needed to "retain" the original (step 1 was already satisfied by the existing
    R1/012 architecture). `triggerSave` now reads `editorRef.current.isDirty()` (the editor's own
    authoritative dirty flag, exposed on `ComposeEditorHandle` — chosen over the local `isDirty`
    React state because that state can lag an in-flight mammoth import per DEF-01) and only calls
    `tipTapToDocxBytes` via `editor.serialize()` when dirty (or defensively, when no original bytes
    were retained); otherwise it sends `state.docxBytes` verbatim. `ComposeService.SaveAsync`
    required NO behavior change — it already treats `Content` as an opaque byte payload persisted
    through the SpeFileStore/`ISpeFileOperations` facade (ADR-007) to whichever container
    create-on-save (013) resolved; a documentation comment was added there to make the invariant
    explicit and point at the new regression test. New test file
    `ComposeServiceUploadFidelityTests.cs` (4 tests) guards BFF-side byte-identity for both the
    create-on-save (Fork B) and replace-existing paths, plus the negative/no-op-edit case.

    Verification: dotnet build 0 errors; Compose-scoped BFF tests 287/287 green (incl. the 4 new);
    full BFF unit suite 8045/8046 pass (1 unrelated pre-existing flake,
    `TenantCacheMetricsTests.GetAsync_MissThenHit_IncrementsMissesThenHits`, confirmed green in
    isolation — a shared-static-counter flake under full-suite parallelism, not touched by this
    task). Compose.Components: `tsc --noEmit` clean; jest 69/69 (8 suites) green — no new client
    test was added (write boundary restricted this task to production code in
    ComposeWorkspace.tsx only, not a new/edited jest file).

    BFF hygiene: publish (Release) compressed 46.56 MB incl. PDBs — well under the 60 MB ceiling
    and ~0 delta attributable to this task (no new packages/dependencies; the absolute number
    differs from the CLAUDE.md-cited 49.63 MB reference point because many other tasks have landed
    on this branch since that baseline was taken). `dotnet list package --vulnerable
    --include-transitive` shows only the pre-existing Kiota HIGH advisory — no NEW HIGH CVE.

    Quality gates (Step 9.5): code-review clean (no Critical/Warning on the ~28-line diff across
    the two production files + the new test file; both touched files are pre-existing large files,
    growth from this task is <2% each). adr-check: no violation attributable to this diff. Ran
    `Spaarke.ArchTests` for completeness — 5 pre-existing failures exist on this branch
    (ADR-007/009/010, all in `Sprk.Bff.Api.Services.Communication.*` / `Api.Office.Errors.*` /
    `Infrastructure.Errors.*` / caching / options-pattern classes) — none reference Compose and
    none are introduced or touched by this task; flagged as pre-existing debt, out of this task's
    scope.

    Deferrals discovered (NOT fixed — out of file-list bounds / separate FRs): (1) `SaveComposeDocumentBody`
    (ComposeEndpoints.cs) has no `containerId` wire field and `ComposeWorkspace.tsx` never sets
    `documentRef.containerId` or sends it on Save — the client→BFF create-on-save (013) `ContainerId`
    plumbing appears incomplete end-to-end; (2) `ComposeToolbar`'s Save button is disabled whenever
    `documentId` is empty (`hasDocument` check), which is always true for a transient
    Browse/Upload mount before its first Save — the Save button cannot be clicked for a brand-new
    unsaved draft (Ctrl+S still works, bypassing the toolbar). Both look like pre-existing gaps in
    task 013's/010's frontend wiring, not introduced here; recommend `/project-defer-issue-tracking`
    entries if not already tracked.
  </notes>
</task>
